# Raising a dispute on the local stack (docker compose up --wait), through the gateway.
# Sign in first, headless: scripts/dev-login.sh customer-a (linked by the seed)
# then copy the disputedesk-session value from the cookie jar it prints into @session below.
# Run "Antiforgery token" first: it sets the disputedesk-antiforgery cookie, so copy that value into @antiforgery.
# Every raise needs an Idempotency-Key: an RFC 9651 String, so quoted, 1 to 255 printable characters (AD-16).
# The same request with the same key gets the stored response again; {{$guid}} gives each request a new key.
# With curl, keep both cookies in the jar:
#   token=$(curl -s -b <jar> -c <jar> http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bff/antiforgery | jq -r .requestToken)
#   curl -b <jar> -H "X-XSRF-TOKEN: $token" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H "Idempotency-Key: \"$(uuidgen)\"" \
#     -d '{"accountRef":"ACC-A-1","transactionId":"TXN-A-0029","reason":"unrecognised"}' http://localhost:8080/api/v1/disputes

@app = http://localhost:8080
@session = paste-the-disputedesk-session-cookie-value
@antiforgery = paste-the-disputedesk-antiforgery-cookie-value
@raiseKey = "replay-demo-1"

### Antiforgery token: the X-XSRF-TOKEN value for unsafe requests
# @name token
GET {{app}}/api/v1/bff/antiforgery
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### Raise: 201 submitted with Location /api/v1/disputes/<disputeId> (TXN-A-0029 is A's settled card debit, 2 days old)
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{raiseKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0029", "reason": "unrecognised", "note": "I did not make this purchase."}

### The same raise with the same key: the stored 201 again, byte for byte, and no second dispute
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{raiseKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0029", "reason": "unrecognised", "note": "I did not make this purchase."}

### A different request under the same key: 422 idempotency-mismatch
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{raiseKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0029", "reason": "duplicateCharge"}

### The same transaction under a new key: 409 already-disputed, carrying the existing dispute's disputeId and customerStatus
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: "{{$guid}}"
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0029", "reason": "duplicateCharge"}

### Wrong amount: the dispute is for the difference (TXN-A-0028 is R259.70, so R59.70)
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: "{{$guid}}"
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0028", "reason": "wrongAmount", "expectedAmount": "200.00"}

### A pending transaction: 422 not-disputable with reason notEligible
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: "{{$guid}}"
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0030", "reason": "unrecognised"}

### An expected amount with another reason: 400 validation naming expectedAmount, before any lookup
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: "{{$guid}}"
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0027", "reason": "unrecognised", "expectedAmount": "10.00"}

### An unquoted key: 400 validation (the key must be an RFC 9651 String)
POST {{app}}/api/v1/disputes
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}; disputedesk-antiforgery={{antiforgery}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.requestToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"accountRef": "ACC-A-1", "transactionId": "TXN-A-0027", "reason": "unrecognised"}

### The transactions list now shows the dispute on TXN-A-0029: disputeId, customerStatus submitted, notDisputableReason alreadyDisputed
GET {{app}}/api/v1/transactions?limit=50
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### History list: the customer's disputes newest first, a page of 1 so nextCursor is set while more follow
# @name history
GET {{app}}/api/v1/disputes?limit=1
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### The next page: the previous page's nextCursor back as cursor; nextCursor is null on the last page
GET {{app}}/api/v1/disputes?limit=1&cursor={{history.response.body.nextCursor}}
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### A cursor no page returned: 400 validation naming cursor, without echoing it
GET {{app}}/api/v1/disputes?cursor=not-a-cursor
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}
